{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>That it may go well with you.</b> Some say it hints at the World to Come, and the mystery of the World to Come we have hinted at in the verse \"I deal death and give life\" (Deuteronomy 32:39)." "<b>Your days.</b> He explained that they will be good. Know that the view of all the ancients is that the first utterance is \"I am\" (anokhi). And if one should ask why the one who made divisions interrupted [before] \"You shall not have,\" I have already explained the Ten Commandments, for I relied on their view. Only it seems right to me that the word anokhi is not one of the ten, for the utterance anokhi is the commandment and the essence of the commandments, as I have already explained."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:25.920444766Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}